# The build context is EMPTY on purpose.
#
# Containerfile has no COPY and no ADD: the checkout is bind-mounted at /repo
# when the container runs (see scripts/build-iso.sh), so the image itself needs
# nothing from here. Without this file `docker build` still uploads the whole
# directory to the daemon before doing anything — which already meant shipping
# the 1.2 GB ISO on every build, and became untenable once the QEMU disk images
# moved into vm/ (tens of gigabytes of them).
#
# If a COPY is ever added to Containerfile, un-ignore exactly what it needs
# rather than deleting this line. Sending the whole tree is never the answer
# here: iso/ and vm/ are both large and both regenerable.
*
